### Page 5 of 12

```text
UDC-13-00271 – Terre Pont Preliminary Plat – Page 5
this property, which is primarily appropriate for general retail and office uses. Secondary uses may
include multifamily housing (apartments). Hotels and motels are a permitted use in the CB zone district.
2 || Existing & Future Development - The application reflects sound planning and urban design
principles with respect to existing and potential future development in the vicinity, including
consideration of current and future streets, open spaces, blocks and lots, and public utilities or facilities.
This criteria appears to be met to the extent applicable. The property is in a problematic area concerning
transportation due to lack of connectivity. Rue Terre extends from the south at Dell Range then ends
north of K-Mart to the east of the subject property. To the north of the subject property Rue Terre curves
north and the west half of the road is constructed behind the shopping center there (Frontier North) and
ends at the north property line of the shopping center. The east half has not been platted or annexed in
that area. Building half of the road width is not a major concern, but connecting Rue Terre through to
the south would be preferable since it would increase connectivity and address the need sooner rather
than later. With an unconstructed gap, some motorists will use it anyway, as can be seen with Cutoff
Road. This will increase pressure on the City to install the road.
3 || Subdivision Standards - The division of land meets the purposes, intent, and all applicable
standards in Article 4.
Article 4, Subdivision Regulations provides standards for coordinating development across different
areas and over time. It addresses development patterns and includes planning, design, and engineering
standards for systems that coordinate development across large areas, including open space,
transportation, and utilities. It is most useful to anyone considering dividing land and public officials
that review development applications in relation to long-range plans and impacts.
4.2 Community Facilities and Fees
The final plat will require payment of park fees as outlined below (subject to change).
