4.3 Transportation Networks and Street Designs
The proposed development complies with the long-range transportation plan, maximum block perimeter, and
maximum and minimum block face lengths. The location of the streets surrounding the subject property is
generally established already. As mentioned previously, sidewalks will need to be installed where they do not
currently exist. The main issue with this project is the timing of the extension of Rue Terre to the south to
where it currently ends behind K-Mart. As proposed, that section of Rue Terre would be constructed when the
adjacent vacant lot (Lot 2, Block 1, Terre Fini) develops. However, this 1.4-acre lot has a triangular shape and
has limited development potential due to its size and shape, having been platted 23 ago. Current UDC
regulations are intended to prevent this type of problem, but this lot was platted in 1990 and options to correct
it are now limited. The Terre Fini property is owned by the current owner of the subject property.
```

