### Page 8 of 12

```text
UDC-13-00271 – Terre Pont Preliminary Plat – Page 8
4.4 Open Space Systems
Open space equivalent to eight percent of the area of the building footprint will be required on-site, which will
be private open space. This requirement will be evaluated during the site plan review.
4 || Phasing Amenities, Facilities - Any phasing proposed in the application is clearly indicated and
demonstrates a logical and well-planned development pattern. This may include consideration of
amenities and public facilities of the subdivision within each phase compared to the anticipated timing
or the likelihood of future phases being constructed as planned.
No development is proposed for Lot 2 at this time, but street improvements will be made to Rue Terre
adjacent to both lots. As mentioned, there will still be a gap southeast of the subject property north of the
Terre Fini lot. As noted in comments below from Engineering, this gap will create pressure on the City
to absorb the cost and construct the remaining portion of Rue Terre in this area. Since the City has not
established impact fees on development for off-site street improvements, any such construction by the
City would be paid for by all taxpayers rather than the development. This conflicts with PlanCheyenne
Foundation 7, which promotes development paying for improvements necessitated by the development.
However, whether the City or the developer pays for the improvements, a reimbursement requirement
could be filed against the adjacent properties so that when they develop they will be required to pay their
share of the improvements.
When development north of Rue Terre occurs Rue Terre will need to be widened to the full width.
No improvements to Cutoff Road are proposed with development of the hotel.
5 || Studies and Reports - The impacts identified in specific studies or technical reports that were
prepared or requested to be prepared in association with the application, and whether the findings and
recommendations of these reports, or any modifications or conditions on approval of the application,
can mitigate these impacts.
A Traffic Impact Study will be required prior to approval of a site plan. Drainage improvements include
extension of an existing stormwater line along Rue Terre. Further review will occur with site plan submittals
when more detailed design plans are submitted.
6 || Zoning - All proposed lots shall be buildable lots according to the existing or proposed zoning
district standards, and result in site design and development patterns that meet the Intent and
Applicability statements of the existing or proposed zoning district. All parcels not proposed as
buildable lots and which are not dedicated to and accepted by the City shall have a clearly defined
entity responsible for ongoing maintenance.
Both lots appear to be developable with the proposed CB zoning.
7 || Adjacent Development - The application will not create any undue influence on existing or
potential development for adjacent property considering the existing zoning and Comprehensive Plan
policies for that property.
The properties to the south and west are already similarly developed. The proposed development should
have a positive effect on adjacent vacant land by extending water and sewer lines and street
improvements.
8 || Health Safety and Welfare - The application is not harmful to the public health, safety, and
welfare.
Development will be required to meet all applicable requirements regarding engineering, building
construction, fire access and hydrants, and food safety, among others.
```

### Page 9 of 12

```text
UDC-13-00271 – Terre Pont Preliminary Plat – Page 9
REVIEWING AGENCIES AND REVIEWER’S COMMENTS:
Board of Public Utilities:
1. The property Owners will be required to extend the sanitary sewer utilities from its current
location to the farthest point (or points) of the property being annexed along Rue Terre. The
exiting 8" water main on the west end of Rue Terre will need to be extended from its current
location to tie into the exiting 12" water on the east end of Rue Terre to complete the water main
loop. These utility extensions shall be to a point (or points) that are logical for projected future
connections to future development projects, as determined by the BOPU and the property
owners/developer.
2. All BOPU's water/sewer utilities shall be located in the City of Cheyenne Street Right-of-Ways
or have the appropriate easements record at the Clerk of Laramie County Real Estate Office or
easements shown on the recorded plat. All water and sanitary sewer utilities need to be designed
and constructed in accordance with the latest City of Cheyenne and Board of Public Utilities
Construction Specifications Standards and Standard Drawings and the latest Rules &
Regulations for Establishing Policies & Design Criteria of the Board of Public Utilities
Cheyenne, Wyoming.
City Surveyor: (Note: These comments will be addressed on the final plat. The preliminary plat is not a
recorded document.)
1. Boundary data appears in order for mathematical closure.
2. A symbol for the SET REBAR W/ALUMINUM CAP called for in the LEGAL DESCRIPTION
at the easterly end of the curve on the northerly boundary is not shown, and is required. Also, the
LEGEND needs to have a symbol and description for these set corners.
3. There are two minor discrepancies between the map data shown and the calls in the LEGAL
DESCRIPTION. FIRST: the distance for the northwesterly boundary course calls for a distance
of 700.75' on the map, but calls for 700.76' in the LEGAL DESCRIPTION; SECOND: the
distance for the long chord of the curve along the easterly boundary calls for 120.48' on the map,
but calls for 120.49' in the LEGAL DESCRIPTION. These discrepancies are required to be
rectified.
4. City Code 1.12.020 - C.1 - 3 requires that two (2) City Control Stations be used for survey ties to
the City Control Ground Datum. Only one (1) City Control Station "YOD" is shown on this plat.
The second station used, must be shown and identified. Also, the published City Ground Datum
coordinates for these Control Stations must be provided as well.
5. City Code 1.12.020 - C.1 - 3 also requires that two (2) monumented corners of one course of the
boundary also have the City Ground Datum coordinates provided. The corner tied to the Control
Stations and the monument on the other end of the first course, generally. If copy of the City
Code is required, please contact us.
6. There is no right of way width provided on the westerly end of Rue Terre, so it is an assumption
that the width is uniform at 140'. The planned dimension is to be provided at said westerly end of
said Rue Terre for this plat.
7. What are the adjacent right of way dimensions for Rue Terre, Frontier Mall Drive, Prairie Ave,
and Cutoff Road?
Development:
1. Note the EIS discusses the benefits of the Rue Terre connection which would be true however
the developer of the Hotel will not be connecting Rue Terre to the existing Rue Terre.
```

### Page 10 of 12

```text
UDC-13-00271 – Terre Pont Preliminary Plat – Page 10
Identification of open space on the plat is not required. Any required open space/landscaping will
be reviewed with the site plan
Engineering, Drainage:
1. Please submit supporting information for all calculations, including (but not limited to):
preliminary site plan exhibit used to determine impervious surfaces (calculations submitted
indicate the site will be less than 42% impervious), graphics showing flow paths used for Time
of Concentrations (Tc), all Tc calculations, all Rational Method calculations, and all detention
calculations.
2. The design of the extension of the storm sewer system in Rue Terre will need to show the City
criteria are being met. This design will also need to provide for offsite runoff to get into the
system.
Engineering, General:
1. When constructed, this project will leave approximately 460 feet of Rue Terre unconstructed
behind K-Mart. This stretch will probably be difficult to keep from becoming an unofficial road
between the two constructed sections. This may result in the City having to incur some expense
to construct the missing piece.
Engineering, Traffic: (Note: Several additional comments regarding the forthcoming site plan were
provided to the applicant.)
1. A Transportation Worksheet to determine TIA/TIS requirements was provided as required (ref.
Article 3, section 3.1.1.c., UDC). The Transportation Worksheet was signed as required. The
number of trips generated appears to be more than the threshold amount which would trigger a
TIA or a TIS, therefore a Transportation Impact Study for this project will be required.
2. All Arterial and Collector streets shall be connected and extended to the boundary of the site (ref.
Article 4, Section 4.3.3.f., UDC).
Environmental Health:
1. Cheyenne-Laramie County Food Rule WY Regulations for Swimming Pools, Spas and Similar
Installations. Any food service or pool/spa shall submit plans directly to this office at least thirty
days prior to the start of construction. A Wyoming Food Service license shall be obtained prior
to selling or giving away any food. A Wyoming Pool/spa license shall be obtained prior to
opening any pool/spa for use.
Fire:
1. Extend water mains and fire hydrant placement to comply with the 2006 International Fire Code,
Appendix "C".
Charter Communications (formerly Optimum):
1. Charter communications has fiber optics in the road ROW at the northwest corner of the
intersection of Prairie Ave and Cutoff Road. This fiber line crosses Prairie from the south to this
corner then crosses Cutoff Road from this corner east to the 10' utility easement along the north
property line of Lot 1, Block 1 of Terre Fini, 2nd Filing.
Parks & Recreation:
1. Disagree with the determination of "0" bicyclists and pedestrians in the TIS.
2. Do not preclude future provision of a direct traffic connection from Prairie to Rue Terre through
Lot 2.
Reviewing Agencies with No Comment:  Engineering Tech/GIS, MPO
Reviewing Agencies Not Responding: CenturyLink, Cheyenne Light, Fuel & Power, City Engineer
